sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sick et al. (2006) & Andl et al. (2002) WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion hair follicle spacing, secondary wave insertion, transgenic phenotypes & (Pass 3) 3D dermal condensate FGF20/BMP4 chemotaxis with hair peg downgrowth faithfully reproduces Embryonic mouse (Mus musculus) epidermal hair follicle placode lattice with dermal condensate formation and hair peg downgrowth; K14-Wnt / Dkk1 / Fgf20-null / BMP4-excess genotypes morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Embryonic mouse (Mus musculus) epidermal hair follicle placode lattice with dermal condensate formation and hair peg downgrowth; K14-Wnt / Dkk1 / Fgf20-null / BMP4-excess genotypes specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 85.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py; output: docs/media/wnt_dkk_hair_follicle_comparison.png; organism: Embryonic mouse (Mus musculus) epidermal hair follicle placode lattice with dermal condensate formation and hair peg downgrowth; K14-Wnt / Dkk1 / Fgf20-null / BMP4-excess genotypes; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/64526a0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 6a8fbee2728c3b1e0b4daa692316d84bdc3d4612b3958090f46312888c4939f9; artifact_sha256: 2ede41f73dae7b113013b9bcf000da0a78ad2ab1a741478e2d31109808de2905; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/wnt_dkk_hair_follicle/hair_follicle_placode_specimen.jpg=f48a7d76ae5984e5..., datasets/wnt_dkk_hair_follicle/paper_citations.bib=7843d2b728a0e537..., datasets/wnt_dkk_hair_follicle/scout_manifest.json=39fe775496e89c51..., datasets/wnt_dkk_hair_follicle/wnt_dkk_hair_follicle_reference.json=6426dc6a46e1c204...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sick et al. (2006): WNT (short-range activator) and DKK (long-range inhibitor) form a Turing/Meinhardt reaction-diffusion pair that sets pelage follicle spacing; K14-Dkk1 overexpression reduces/abolishes follicles, altered WNT/DKK balance enlarges or crowds placodes, and a secondary follicle wave inserts between primary follicles as the skin grows | Andl et al. (2002): ectopic Dkk1 blocks follicle initiation (no placodes) | Huh et al. (2013): placode-derived FGF20 is required for primary and secondary dermal condensates; Fgf20-null placodes form but do not progress | Glover et al. (2017): dermal cells aggregate directly beneath placodes by directed migration toward placode FGF20 | Botchkarev et al. (1999), Mou et al. (2006): BMP4 inhibits follicle induction / dermal condensation; Noggin/EDA antagonise it | Paus et al. (1999): ordinal morphological stages placode -> hair germ (with DC) -> hair peg; reconstructed_in_script: Saturating Gierer-Meinhardt WNT/DKK PDE with exact steady state, Jacobian and d_c = (sqrt2+1)^2; 1D primary wave -> 2x expansion -> secondary insertion (4 -> 8); 2D WT / K14-Wnt / enlarged / Dkk1 / equal-diffusion regimes; Dkk1 dosage and domain-length sweeps; optical-density segmentation of the vendored specimen | (Pass 3) 3D dermal slab beneath the WT placode field: FGF20 sourced at z = 0 by the placodes, BMP4 produced by the dermis, Keller-Segel chemotaxis with volume filling in conservative face-flux form, per-placode hair-peg depth ODE, WT / Fgf20-null / chemotaxis-null / BMP4-excess genotypes, chi_f sweep, dermal linear stability, seam-aware placode counting; transfer_boundary: All parameters are dimensionless and chosen to produce the qualitative regimes; none of D_w, D_h, mu, rho, kappa, D_f, mu_f, chi_f, chi_b, D_rho, v_peg is traced to a measured value or to Sick et al.'s SOM parameter table | The vendored specimen is a Gad1 whole-mount in situ of E12.5-E13.5 vibrissa/hair placodes (Maddox & Condie 2004), not a pelage pattern from Sick et al.; the PDE lattice (15 placodes, NN-spacing CV 0.086) and the specimen (16 segmented placodes, CV 0.323) agree in count only approximately and disagree in regularity | The K14-Wnt regime changes D_w, D_h and kappa together with rho_w, so it is a 'denser lattice' preset rather than a pure WNT-overexpression perturbation | The dermal coupling is one-way (placodes -> dermis); the epidermis stays planar and peg downgrowth is a scalar depth per placode; stage thresholds 25%/50% of slab depth are a model convention; does_not_claim: A deforming epithelial interface or tissue mechanics of invagination, DC -> epidermis feedback (DC-derived Noggin/FGF), follicle-type specification by DC size, calibration of slab depth or peg depth to micrometres, or numerical parity with Sick et al.'s own simulation parameters]; other sources: Volume-filling and quorum-sensing in models for chemosensitive movement <https://www.math.ualberta.ca/~thillen/paper/Painter-Hillen.pdf>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(70)90092-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S1534-5807(02)00167-3>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/11078>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1046/j.1523-1747.1999.00740.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0600825103>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.198945.112>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1130088>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-4-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.2002117> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.859"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "2002-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "64526a0" .
}

